+ * _GNW_win_refresh copies the window's buffer into _screen_buffer, then this
+ * copies _screen_buffer into gSdlSurface, and then SDL_BlitSurface turns
+ * gSdlSurface into the panel's pixels.  Three passes over a quarter of a
+ * megabyte, of which the middle one exists only because the original port
+ * kept an eight-bit staging surface beside the screen buffer that already
+ * holds exactly the same pixels in exactly the same layout.
